#import "../../lib/24xx.typ": *

#show: xx.with(
  title: "AX&X: The Sky-Anchor of Aethelgard",
  subtitle: "A fantasy adventure for AX&X, for 4 to 6 characters of levels 4 to 5",
  cols: 2,
)

= The Hook

A frantic gnome named Pipkin, Archivist of Oakhaven, hires the party on the strength of a torn star-chart. It points to the Cloud-Spires, a range of floating peaks that broke from the mainland during the Great Sundering and drifted off centuries ago. Pipkin is sure the _Sovereign of the Zephyr_, a gnomish airship that once crossed oceans in days, still sits docked at the highest spire, held in an old stasis field. He offers #k[1,000 GP] for its safe return, and first claim on whatever else the party can carry off.

= Act I: The Ascent

The party starts at the foot of the Cloud-Spires and has to reach the floating islands.

- #item[The Gravity Lift][A massive stone platform, powered by a dormant elemental core, still stands at the base. Wake the core and it will carry the party up.]
- #item[The Gargoyles][A colony of gargoyles roosts on the platform and treats it as an ancestral throne. Their chieftain wants a tribute of gems or a tale of real bravery before he lets anyone pass. Offer one and the party rolls Reaction at +2; refuse and they fight for the control crystals.]
- #item[The Rise][Starting the lift trips an alarm in the spire above. As the platform climbs through the mist, harpies swoop in and sing, trying to coax characters off the edge.]

= Act II: The Spire of Whispers

The lift reaches a jagged island of obsidian and marble, overgrown with glowing flora. The way to the airship runs up through the Spire of Whispers, a vertical dungeon of crumbling libraries and floating stairs.

- #item[Weightless Zones][Some halls have lost their gravity. Crossing one is a #k[STR or DEX Check, 12+], or you drift into the ceiling spikes or out into open air.]
- #item[Wraith-Librarians][The spire is haunted by wraiths that attack anyone who reads the forbidden scrolls. A wraith can hush a caster: #k[Will save] or no casting for 1d4 rounds. They are harmed only by magic or silver.]
- #item[The Solar Mirrors][The hangar doors open only to concentrated moonlight. Three mirrors on three platforms must be turned to throw the beam into a central prism, each a character's action, while Clockwork Sentinels come in waves. Three aligned beams and the doors grind open.]

= Act III: The Sovereign of the Zephyr

Beyond the doors waits the _Sovereign of the Zephyr_, a ship of brass and mahogany. It is not empty.

- #item[Thalros][A cloud giant has claimed the ship as his hoard. He has no wish to sail it. He lounges on its deck and keeps the crew's preserved bodies as furniture.]
- #item[The Deck Fight][The battle plays out on the open deck. Thalros wakes the ship's last working systems to call up small thunderstorms that shove the party toward the rail.]
- #item[The Failing Engine][The Aether-Engine is unstable. Every few rounds the deck heaves: #k[Dodge save] or slide 20 ft in a random direction. Over the rail is a long fall.]
- #item[The Navigator][With Thalros down, one riddle remains, etched into the helm. Solve it with an #k[INT Check, 12+] or with good talk, and the ship's sleeping spirit wakes. The crew called it the Navigator.]

= The Choice

The Navigator opens its eyes and asks whose orders it follows now. The party has three ways to go.

+ Keep the _Sovereign_. It answers to the party, but Pipkin's claim and the approaching fleet both come due.
+ Hand the ship to Pipkin and Oakhaven. Collect the pay and a standing welcome in the gnome-halls.
+ Let the Navigator steer its own course. It grants the party one voyage anywhere in thanks, then lifts off alone.

= Rewards

Pipkin pays the promised #k[1,000 GP] the moment the chart proves true. Keep the _Sovereign_ and the party holds a ship that crosses oceans in days, though its Aether-Engine wants a gnomish wright's care after every long haul.

Either way, a fleet of hired blades now knows the ship was found, and the open sky ahead is not empty.

= Threats

#k[HD] Hit Dice, #k[AC] Armor Class, #k[Atk] attack bonus and damage. Attack bonus equals HD.

- #item[Gargoyle][HD 4, HP 18, AC 16, Atk +4 (1d6 claws). Flies. A construct: immune to Sleep, Charmed, Poisoned, and Frightened. Resistant to all but magic weapons.]
- #item[Gargoyle Chieftain][HD 6, HP 28, AC 17, Atk +6 (1d8 claws). Flies. As a gargoyle, but proud, and open to tribute.]
- #item[Harpy][HD 3, HP 13, AC 13, Atk +3 (1d4 talons). Flies. Song: Will save or walk toward the harpy, even off a ledge, until struck.]
- #item[Wraith-Librarian][HD 5, HP 22, AC 15, Atk +5 (1d6 chilling touch, Body save or Injured). Harmed only by magic or silver. Can hush a caster for 1d4 rounds on a failed Will save.]
- #item[Clockwork Sentinel][HD 4, HP 20, AC 17, Atk +4 (1d8 blade). A construct: immune to Sleep, Charmed, Poisoned, and Frightened. Vulnerable to lightning.]
- #item[Thalros, Cloud Giant][HD 8, HP 40, AC 17, Atk +8 (2d8 slam). Thunder-call: a 20 ft burst, Dodge save or 3d6 and shoved to the deck's edge.]
